  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Dry conditions will persist through the weekend \nwith rain chances increasing early next week. \n\nRidging aloft will remain the driving feature across the \nSoutheast U.S. through the weekend. Dry high pressure will be \nsituated directly across the forecast area this afternoon then \nwill gradually shift east out into the Atlantic through the \nweekend. Temperatures will be typical of early summer with upper\n80s/lower 90s with the potential for some mid 90s by Sunday and\nMonday. Overnight lows will gradually warm each night, with \nupper 60s/lower 70s inland with lower/mid 70s at beaches and\nDowntown Charleston into early next week.\n\nRain chances will begin to increase early next week as a \nweakness develops in the ridge and the area of broad subsidence \nlessens across the region. This result in a more typical, \ndiurnally driven pattern of showers/tstms from Tuesday onward. A\nweak cold front could approach from the north Tuesday, but model\ntrends suggest the front may dissipate prior to reaching the\nSouth Santee River.",
